    "text_full": "Skip to content\nAbout Us\nPrograms\nNews & Media\nDONATE\nFR\nHERITAGE MINUTES\nPODCASTS\nVIDEOS\nEDUCATION GUIDES\nSEARCH PRODUCTIONS\nHome\n / Podcasts / Strong & Free Podcast\nStrong & Free Podcast\n\nTracing stories from the earliest Black settlers to recently arrived Canadians, Strong and Free captures just a few of the crucial stories of Black Canadians thriving and contributing to building this country.\n\nFeatures\nEpisode 5 | Strong and Free | John Ware: The Legend of Canada’s ‘First’ Black Cowboy\nPopular\nKnown for his strength and horsemanship and his innovative ranching techniques, John Ware was a legendary Albertan.\nEpisode 4 | Strong and Free | Mary Ann Shadd: Journalism, Activism, and the Power of Words\nFeatured\nIn this episode, we have the pleasure of speaking with two of Shadd’s descendants: Marishana Mabusela, our researcher for this podcast, and her mother, writer and historian Adrienne Shadd.\nEpisode 2 | Strong and Free | Herb Carnegie: Black Excellence on – and off – the Ice\nStaff Pick\nHerb Carnegie is widely regarded as the best Black player to never play in the NHL.\nAll (6) Episodes\nSort by:\nDate\nA to Z\nSearch & Filter\nEpisode 6 | Strong and Free | Haitian Diaspora in Quebec: Rhymes and Revolution\n2021\nEpisode 5 | Strong and Free | John Ware: The Legend of Canada’s ‘First’ Black Cowboy\n2021\nEpisode 4 | Strong and Free | Mary Ann Shadd: Journalism, Activism, and the Power of Words\n2021\nEpisode 3 | Strong and Free | Marie-Josèphe Angélique : Montreal on Fire\n2021\nEpisode 2 | Strong and Free | Herb Carnegie: Black Excellence on – and off – the Ice\n2021\nEpisode 1| Strong and Free | West Indian Domestic Scheme: Nurturing a Nation\n2021\n\nHistorica Canada is a charitable organization that offers programs in both official languages that you can use to explore, learn, reflect on our history, and consider what it means to be Canadian.\n\nHistorica Canada's business number is 885434720RR0001\n\nAbout Us\nPolicies\nCareers\nHistorica Canada Content Usage Request Form\n\nFollow Us\nMore From Historica Canada\nCitizenship Challenge\nHeritage Minutes\nThe Memory Project\nThe Canadian Encyclopedia\nPartnership: The World Remembers\n© Historica Canada 2026. All rights reserved.\nWebsite by DS"
